From: NeiroNext <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:42:54 +0000
Subject: Ask the shell for the end-session dialog when Cinnamon is not
 running

cinnamon-session asks Cinnamon (org.Cinnamon) to show the end-session
dialog and falls back to its own Gtk dialog when Cinnamon is absent. A
session that runs cinnamon-session under another shell - Ubuntu Unity
does - then gets two dialogs for one shutdown: the shell's, then
cinnamon-session's.

gnome-session, which cinnamon-session was forked from, asks the shell
through the org.gnome.SessionManager.EndSessionDialog interface on
org.gnome.Shell, which shells other than gnome-shell implement too (Unity
7 does). When org.Cinnamon cannot be reached and such a shell is present,
do what gnome-session does: run the query-end-session phase, then call
the shell's Open with the inhibitors, and act on its answer - Confirmed*
ends the session, Canceled cancels it. The Gtk dialog remains the
fallback when neither shell answers. Nothing changes under Cinnamon: the
first branch is taken as before.

Without org.Cinnamon the call fails with ServiceUnknown rather than
NameHasNoOwner, because the proxy may auto-start; both mean the same here.

Assisted-by: LLM claude-opus-5-5
